ary of president  eisenhower mr bayar who recalled mr  nixon's hospitality when he himself  visited washington insisted that the  vice president and his wife be his  personal guests  [Music]  next day there were more of those chance  meetings with ordinary people a brief  chat with a young turkish news boy  brought out his deep interest in america  and his affection for president  eisenhower  these were feelings that mr nixon  noticed everywhere he went and in people  from widely different backgrounds and  national origins  [Music]  one of the most impressive moments of  vice president nixon's stay in the  turkish capital was his laying of a  wreath at the tomb of kemal ataturk the  founder of modern turkey  the second highest official of the  united states government paid a solemn  salute to the memory of one of the most  extraordinary leaders of this century  driving back to the city enroute to the  airport the american vice president's  motorcade stopped in the center of uluz  an ancient historic part of ankara  this gave mr nixon the opportunity once  more to meet the people he stepped out  and shook hands with many persons who  quickly surrounded his car  [Music]  at the airport there was one last  friendly touch  vice president and mrs nixon had a  personal goodbye for the police officers  who escorted them  a final farewell from the chief of the  national assembly and from premier  mandarin for whom mr nixon carried a  message to president eisenhower  then the vice president's plane turned  westward once more over the capital city  and over turkey that ancient land which  is at once so modern too  [Music]  at palma in the spanish mediterranean  island of mallorca the plane stopped  briefly to refuel vice president nixon  was greeted by the u.s ambassador to  spain john lodge and by spanish foreign  minister alberto martinez  last refueling stop was bermuda in the  mid-atlantic then 11 days after they had  left home vice president and mrs nixon  returned to washington  a large crowd greeted them including  senator noland and secretary of state  dulles  and historic tour was over  reassurances of east west friendship had  been made around the world especially  with six nations whom the united states  is proud to call partners in the  struggle for freedom  weekends on c-span 2
 

